IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `we57-nouns`

-- Row il-57. THE THREE ITEMS, as typed values.
-- A citation is encoded as TWO descriptions: what the citing words say they point at, and what the target is. A test compares them. Where they differ, the citation does not point at what it says;
-- that is a defect, kept in an expected-red file with its count declared in check.sh and encoding.json.
-- A list is also encoded with the subsection the amending instrument added, whether the citing words name it, and the first day the amending instrument is read to have taken effect.
-- ITEM 1 (a list of extensions). DEFECT: section 6(ב)(2) defines "הארכות" by listing sections 6(ב1), (ג) and (ד); Amendment 67 added an extension in a new section 6(ד3) and put it into the cumulation rule (ד2), not into the definition.
--   CONTROL 1: the cumulation rule (ד2), which names (ד3). Two places use the defined term (6(ח)(1א) and 7(ד)(1)) and are recorded as the definition's dependants; two other lists, 6(ז1)(2) and 9ג(ב), stop short of (ד3).
--   Whether those two lists should name (ד3) is a POLICY question that this row does not answer (fork R3 in NOTES.md).
-- ITEM 2 (a list of subsections). DEFECT: section 51(ד) of the National Insurance Law fixes the payment date of the additional maternity allowance of subsections (א) and (א1); Amendment 67 added (א3), which gives the same kind of allowance.
--   CONTROL 2: the new (א3), which cites section 6(ד3) of the Law; the target exists as Amendment 67 inserted it.
-- ITEM 3 (a pronoun). DEFECT: the replacement words for the five-day limb of the paragraph quoted as section 9(ג)(2ג)(א) of the Law say "שהיא הוצאה", a feminine form, in a paragraph whose head names "עובד או עובדת".
--   CONTROL 3: the same replacement made for the National Insurance Law's definition, whose noun is "עובד", reads the masculine form (the ext: lines for printed p. 562 below).
-- LIMBS. Limb (a) is the question whether the target, or the text the citing words belong to, is as the citing words need; limb (b) is the question whether the citing words still read so in the latest official text.
-- Each limb says where it was read from (see `Where a reading comes from` in we57-nouns.l4). The Hebrew Wikisource texts are not official.
-- THE DAY. Amendment 67 says (section 3) that it takes effect "on the 1st of the month after the end of 60 days from its publication"; the issue is dated 7 January 2026, 60 days from that day end on 7 or 8 March 2026
-- by either usual count, so the first of the next month is 1 April 2026. That is the BUILDER'S computation from the printed sentence, not a printed date (fork D1 in NOTES.md); its inputs are on the ext: lines below.
-- A date for which the sources held give no answer is NOTHING; there is no REFUSE.

§ `Cross-references`

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the citation points at what it says` MEANS c's `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS c's `the target is`

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both limbs were read from the official instruments` MEANS
    c's `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
    AND c's `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`

-- Whether the citing words name every subsection the amended text has on a day. Before the amending instrument takes effect the added subsection is not in the text, so there is nothing to name (JUST TRUE);
-- from that day the answer is whether the citing words name it. If the sources give no day for the instrument the answer is NOTHING.
GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the citing words are complete on` MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the amending instrument takes effect on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST first THEN IF day AT LEAST first THEN JUST (c's `the citing words name that subsection`) ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Pronouns`

GIVEN g IS A `Grammatical gender`
      gs IS A LIST OF `Grammatical gender`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every gender in the list is` MEANS
    CONSIDER gs
        WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
        WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN x EQUALS g AND `every gender in the list is` g rest

GIVEN g IS A `Grammatical gender`
      gs IS A LIST OF `Grammatical gender`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some gender in the list is` MEANS
    CONSIDER gs
        WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
        WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN x EQUALS g OR `some gender in the list is` g rest

GIVEN p IS A `A pronoun in replacement words`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the pronoun fits every noun the head names` MEANS
    `every gender in the list is` (p's `the gender of the pronoun and its verb`) (p's `the nouns the head of the paragraph names`)

GIVEN p IS A `A pronoun in replacement words`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the pronoun fits some noun the head names` MEANS
    `some gender in the list is` (p's `the gender of the pronoun and its verb`) (p's `the nouns the head of the paragraph names`)

